# SELECT50 example: ORCA minimum optimization + numerical frequencies with UMA.
#
# SETUP
# 1. Install ORCA 6 and its platform-specific runtime requirements:
#    https://www.faccts.de/docs/orca/6.1/manual/
# 2. Install ORCA External Tools with UMA support using Python >=3.11:
#    git clone https://github.com/faccts/orca-external-tools.git
#    cd orca-external-tools
#    python install.py -e uma --venv-dir .venv-uma --script-dir bin-uma
#    Follow that project's UMA/model-access and PyTorch/CUDA setup instructions.
#    Keep its environment at the installation location; wrappers refer to it.
# 3. Replace ProgExt below with the FULL path to the installed oet_client
#    wrapper (oet_client.exe on Windows). Use forward slashes in this input.
#    Add the wrapper directory to PATH, or use full paths in the commands below.
# 4. In a separate terminal, start the UMA server and leave it running:
#    oet_server uma -b 127.0.0.1:20001 -n 4
#    The loopback address is generic; server and client must use the same port.
#    Check oet_server --help for resource settings supported by your version.
#
# RUN
# Copy this input and your geometry as molecule.xyz into a fresh job directory.
# XYZ coordinates are in angstrom. Edit the final line's charge/multiplicity
# (0 1 = neutral singlet) for your molecule. Select cuda or cpu in Ext_Params.
# Four processes are an example allocation; adjust nprocs and server resources.
# From the job directory, using your installed ORCA executable's full path:
#   /path/to/orca job_orca.inp > job_orca.out 2>&1
# Windows PowerShell syntax for a quoted executable path:
#   & "C:/path/to/orca.exe" job_orca.inp > job_orca.out 2>&1
#
# This retains the supplied UMA-S-1.1/OMol settings and minimum optimization.
# It is not a TS-search or reference-DFT input. NumFREQ requests numerical
# frequencies after optimization; inspect convergence and the resulting modes.
# Retain the input/output, server log, software versions and checkpoint identity
# with results. This example does not establish settings for other deposited jobs.
# External-method setup: https://github.com/faccts/orca-external-tools
#
! ExtOpt TIGHTOPT NumFREQ

%method
  ProgExt "/path/to/oet_client"
  Ext_Params "-b 127.0.0.1:20001 --model uma-s-1p1 --task omol --device cuda"
end

%pal
  nprocs 4
end

%geom
  MaxStep 0.2
  MaxIter 1000
end

* xyzfile 0 1 molecule.xyz
